WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.159 --> 00:00:08.694
<i>( Theme music playing )</i>

2
00:00:08.719 --> 00:00:12.719
<font color=#00FF00>♪ Game of Thrones 2x01 ♪</font>
<font color=#00FFFF>The North Remembers</font>
Original Air Date on April 1. 2012

3
00:00:12.744 --> 00:00:16.744
== sync. corrected by <font color="#00ff00">elderman</font> ==

4
00:00:16.769 --> 00:01:52.475
♪

5
00:02:12.517 --> 00:02:14.952
Well struck.

6
00:02:14.986 --> 00:02:16.754
Well struck. Dog.

7
00:02:20.558 --> 00:02:22.493
Did you like that?

8
00:02:22.527 --> 00:02:24.394
It was well struck.
Your Grace.

9
00:02:24.429 --> 00:02:26.764
I already said
it was well struck.

10
00:02:27.999 --> 00:02:30.134
Yes. Your Grace.

11
00:02:37.576 --> 00:02:39.711
- Who's next?
<i>- Lothor Brune.</i>

12
00:02:39.745 --> 00:02:43.215
freerider in the service
of Lord Baelish.

13
00:02:43.249 --> 00:02:46.685
Ser Dontos the Red
of House Hollard.

14
00:02:49.356 --> 00:02:52.191
Ser Dontos the Red
of House Hollard!

15
00:02:52.226 --> 00:02:53.760
<i>Here I am.</i>

16
00:02:53.794 --> 00:02:56.563
Here I am.

17
00:03:01.902 --> 00:03:04.503
Sorry. Your Grace.

18
00:03:04.537 --> 00:03:06.338
My deepest apologies.

19
00:03:06.372 --> 00:03:08.139
<i>- Are you drunk?</i>
- No.

20
00:03:08.174 --> 00:03:10.876
Uh. no.
No. Your Grace.

21
00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:13.678
- I had two cups of wine.
- Two cups?

22
00:03:13.712 --> 00:03:15.881
That's not much at all.

23
00:03:15.915 --> 00:03:18.383
Please.
have another cup.

24
00:03:18.418 --> 00:03:19.785
Are you sure. Your Grace?

25
00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:22.121
<i>Yes. To celebrate</i>
<i>my name day.</i>

26
00:03:22.156 --> 00:03:24.858
Have two.
Have as much as you like.

27
00:03:24.892 --> 00:03:27.829
I would be honored.
Your Grace.

28
00:03:29.231 --> 00:03:32.300
Ser Meryn. help Ser Dontos
celebrate my name day.

29
00:03:32.334 --> 00:03:34.635
See that he drinks
his fill.

30
00:03:52.187 --> 00:03:55.223
You can't.

31
00:03:55.257 --> 00:03:57.024
What did you say?

32
00:03:58.193 --> 00:04:00.060
Did you say I can't?

33
00:04:00.095 --> 00:04:02.763
I only meant
it would be bad luck

34
00:04:02.797 --> 00:04:04.531
to kill a man
on your name day.

35
00:04:04.565 --> 00:04:06.832
What kind of stupid
peasant's superstition...

36
00:04:06.867 --> 00:04:08.701
<i>The girl is right.</i>

37
00:04:08.735 --> 00:04:10.502
<i>What a man sows</i>
<i>on his name day</i>

38
00:04:10.537 --> 00:04:12.071
he reaps all year.

39
00:04:14.608 --> 00:04:17.243
Take him away.

40
00:04:17.277 --> 00:04:19.512
I'll have him killed
tomorrow. the fool.

41
00:04:22.449 --> 00:04:24.050
He is.

42
00:04:24.084 --> 00:04:25.752
A fool--
you're so clever to see it.

43
00:04:25.786 --> 00:04:29.189
He'll make a much better fool
than a knight.

44
00:04:29.223 --> 00:04:32.526
He doesn't deserve
the mercy of a quick death.

45
00:04:33.895 --> 00:04:36.763
Did you hear My Lady.
Ser Dontos?

46
00:04:36.798 --> 00:04:39.934
From this day.
you'll be my new fool.

47
00:04:39.968 --> 00:04:42.136
Thank you. Your Grace.

48
00:04:42.171 --> 00:04:45.406
And you. My Lady.
thank you.

49
00:04:45.441 --> 00:04:48.410
<i>Beloved nephew.</i>

50
00:04:54.617 --> 00:04:57.318
We looked for you
on the battlefield.

51
00:04:59.254 --> 00:05:02.656
You were nowhere
to be found.

52
00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:05.392
I've been here.
ruling the kingdoms.

53
00:05:05.426 --> 00:05:08.828
What a fine job
you've done.

54
00:05:08.862 --> 00:05:10.496
Look at you.

55
00:05:11.798 --> 00:05:13.933
More beautiful
than ever.

56
00:05:13.967 --> 00:05:18.137
And you! You-- you're going to be
bigger than the hound.

57
00:05:18.171 --> 00:05:20.639
but much better looking.

58
00:05:20.674 --> 00:05:22.575
This one doesn't like me.

59
00:05:22.609 --> 00:05:24.444
Can't imagine why.

60
00:05:24.478 --> 00:05:27.113
- We heard you were dead.
- I'm glad you're not dead.

61
00:05:27.148 --> 00:05:29.049
Me. too. dear.

62
00:05:29.083 --> 00:05:31.351
Death is so boring.
especially now

63
00:05:31.385 --> 00:05:34.388
with so much excitement
in the world.

64
00:05:34.422 --> 00:05:36.658
My Lady. I'm sorry
for your loss.

65
00:05:38.093 --> 00:05:39.728
Her loss?

66
00:05:39.762 --> 00:05:41.663
Her father was
a confessed traitor.

67
00:05:41.697 --> 00:05:43.298
But still her father.

68
00:05:43.333 --> 00:05:45.334
Surely having so recently
lost your own beloved father

69
00:05:45.368 --> 00:05:47.269
you can sympathize.

70
00:05:51.074 --> 00:05:53.208
My father was a traitor.

71
00:05:53.242 --> 00:05:55.109
My mother and brother
are traitors. too.

72
00:05:55.144 --> 00:05:58.346
I am loyal
to my beloved Joffrey.

73
00:05:59.548 --> 00:06:01.949
Of course you are.

74
00:06:03.585 --> 00:06:07.454
Well. enjoy your name day.
Your Grace.

75
00:06:07.489 --> 00:06:09.389
Wish I could stay
and celebrate.

76
00:06:09.424 --> 00:06:12.192
but there is work
to be done.

77
00:06:12.226 --> 00:06:14.227
What work?

78
00:06:14.262 --> 00:06:16.396
Why are you here?

79
00:06:19.266 --> 00:06:22.501
The raven arrived
from the Citadel

80
00:06:22.535 --> 00:06:25.671
- this morning. Your Grace.

81
00:06:25.705 --> 00:06:28.574
The conclave has met.
considered reports

82
00:06:28.608 --> 00:06:30.743
from Maesters all over
the Seven Kingdoms.

83
00:06:30.778 --> 00:06:34.213
<i>and declared</i>
<i>this great summer</i>

84
00:06:34.247 --> 00:06:37.049
done at last.

85
00:06:37.084 --> 00:06:39.886
The longest summer
in living memory.

86
00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:41.888
The peasants say.
a long summer means

87
00:06:41.922 --> 00:06:44.825
- <i>an even longer winter.</i>
<i>- A common superstition.</i>

88
00:06:44.859 --> 00:06:47.895
<i>We have enough wheat</i>
<i>for a five-year winter.</i>

89
00:06:47.929 --> 00:06:50.197
If it lasts any longer.

90
00:06:50.231 --> 00:06:52.865
we'll have
fewer peasants.

91
00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:55.868
The city's drowning in refugees.
Your Grace. fleeing the war.

92
00:06:55.902 --> 00:06:57.369
We have nowhere
to house them.

93
00:06:57.403 --> 00:06:59.538
And with winter coming.
it'll only get worse.

94
00:06:59.572 --> 00:07:02.507
You command the City Watch.
do you not. Lord Slynt?

95
00:07:04.010 --> 00:07:05.877
<i>I do. Your Grace.</i>

96
00:07:05.912 --> 00:07:07.913
And are you not
a Lord at my command?

97
00:07:07.947 --> 00:07:11.450
I owe my title and lands
to your generosity. Your Grace.

98
00:07:11.485 --> 00:07:14.120
Then do your job.
Shut the gates to the peasants.

99
00:07:14.154 --> 00:07:17.089
They belong in the field.
not our capital.

100
00:07:17.124 --> 00:07:20.526
Yes. Your Grace.

101
00:07:25.231 --> 00:07:26.865
Don't get up.

102
00:07:28.034 --> 00:07:31.803
More ravishing than ever.
big sister.

103
00:07:32.872 --> 00:07:35.607
War agrees with you.

104
00:07:35.642 --> 00:07:38.543
Forgive the interruption.
Carry on.

105
00:07:39.778 --> 00:07:41.179
What are you doing here?

106
00:07:41.213 --> 00:07:44.915
Ah. it's been
a remarkable journey.

107
00:07:44.949 --> 00:07:48.619
I pissed off the edge
of the Wall.

108
00:07:48.653 --> 00:07:51.555
<i>I slept in a sky cell.</i>

109
00:07:51.589 --> 00:07:53.824
I fought with
the hill tribes--

110
00:07:53.859 --> 00:07:56.594
so many adventures.

111
00:07:56.628 --> 00:07:59.331
so much to be
thankful for.

112
00:07:59.365 --> 00:08:02.635
What are you doing here?
This is the small council.

113
00:08:03.397 --> 00:08:04.997
Yes. well I. do believe.
the Hand of the King.

114
00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:07.941
is welcome at all
small council meetings.

115
00:08:07.975 --> 00:08:09.977
Our father
is Hand of the King.

116
00:08:10.011 --> 00:08:13.047
Yes. but in his absence...

117
00:08:20.221 --> 00:08:22.456
<i>Your father has named</i>
<i>Lord Tyrion</i>

118
00:08:22.491 --> 00:08:25.226
to serve as Hand
in his stead while he fights.

119
00:08:25.260 --> 00:08:27.928
Out! All of you out!

120
00:08:32.601 --> 00:08:35.303
I would like to know
how you tricked father into this.

121
00:08:35.337 --> 00:08:37.305
If I were capable
of tricking father.

122
00:08:37.339 --> 00:08:38.940
I'd be emperor
of the world by now.

123
00:08:38.974 --> 00:08:41.576
You brought this
on yourself.

124
00:08:41.610 --> 00:08:43.077
I've done nothing.

125
00:08:43.112 --> 00:08:44.979
Quite right--
you did nothing

126
00:08:45.014 --> 00:08:47.381
when your son called
for Ned Stark's head.

127
00:08:47.416 --> 00:08:49.383
Now the entire North
has risen up against us.

128
00:08:49.418 --> 00:08:51.886
- I tried to stop it.
- Did you? You failed.

129
00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:55.056
That bit of theater will haunt
our family for a generation.

130
00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:59.093
- Robb Stark is a child.
- Who's won every battle he's fought.

131
00:08:59.127 --> 00:09:01.329
Do you understand
we're losing the war?

132
00:09:01.363 --> 00:09:04.599
- What do you know about warfare?
- Nothing.

133
00:09:04.633 --> 00:09:06.401
But I know people.

134
00:09:06.435 --> 00:09:08.503
And I know that our enemies hate
each other

135
00:09:08.537 --> 00:09:11.439
almost as much
as they hate us.

136
00:09:15.745 --> 00:09:18.380
- Joffrey is King.
- Joffrey is King.

137
00:09:18.414 --> 00:09:20.949
You are here
to advise him.

138
00:09:20.983 --> 00:09:22.651
I'm only here
to advise him.

139
00:09:22.685 --> 00:09:25.220
And if the King listens
to what I say.

140
00:09:25.255 --> 00:09:28.890
the King might just get
his Uncle Jaime back.

141
00:09:30.593 --> 00:09:32.093
How?

142
00:09:32.128 --> 00:09:33.695
You love your children.

143
00:09:33.729 --> 00:09:35.229
It's your one
redeeming quality.

144
00:09:35.263 --> 00:09:38.198
That and your cheekbones.

145
00:09:38.233 --> 00:09:41.067
The Starks love
their children as well.

146
00:09:41.102 --> 00:09:43.703
- And we have two of them.
- One.

147
00:09:45.306 --> 00:09:48.274
- One?
- Arya. little animal-- she disappeared.

148
00:09:48.309 --> 00:09:51.344
Disappeared?
What. in a puff of smoke?

149
00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:56.416
We had three Starks
to trade.

150
00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:59.186
You chopped one's head off
and let another escape.

151
00:10:00.088 --> 00:10:02.188
Father will be furious.

152
00:10:03.257 --> 00:10:04.858
It must be odd for you...

153
00:10:07.362 --> 00:10:09.663
to be the disappointing child.

154
00:10:17.173 --> 00:10:21.009
<i>My Lord. may the Old Gods</i>
<i>watch over your brother</i>

155
00:10:21.044 --> 00:10:23.712
<i>and all our northern sons.</i>

156
00:10:23.747 --> 00:10:27.716
<i>The walls of my Holdfast</i>
<i>will not stand the winter.</i>

157
00:10:27.751 --> 00:10:31.620
The stones were last mortared
in the time of King Aerys.

158
00:10:31.654 --> 00:10:34.022
and I'm afraid
the masons today

159
00:10:34.056 --> 00:10:37.792
are not fit to carry
their fathers' hammers.

160
00:10:37.826 --> 00:10:40.227
When I was a boy.
I remember seeing them

161
00:10:40.262 --> 00:10:44.831
<i>put up a new tower</i>
<i>at Torrhen's Square in a summer.</i>

162
00:10:44.866 --> 00:10:46.967
<i>Men worked back then.</i>

163
00:10:47.001 --> 00:10:49.903
Today. my Holdfast
looks like it was built

164
00:10:49.938 --> 00:10:52.172
by drunk children.

165
00:10:52.207 --> 00:10:56.344
At night you can hear the wind
howling through the gaps.

166
00:10:56.378 --> 00:10:58.346
<i>And the Gods</i>
<i>forbid it rains.</i>

167
00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:01.616
Why. I might as well sleep
beneath a waterfall.

168
00:11:01.650 --> 00:11:03.285
<i>Maintenance of a Holdfast</i>

169
00:11:03.319 --> 00:11:06.722
generally falls
to the lord of that Holdfast.

170
00:11:06.757 --> 00:11:08.224
Generally. yes.

171
00:11:08.258 --> 00:11:09.925
but I've sent
all the young men off

172
00:11:09.959 --> 00:11:11.861
to fight
Robb Stark's war.

173
00:11:11.895 --> 00:11:14.997
King Robb.
And it's not his war.

174
00:11:15.031 --> 00:11:16.932
He didn't choose it.

175
00:11:16.966 --> 00:11:18.400
Maybe not. My Lord.

176
00:11:18.434 --> 00:11:20.535
but he called in his Banners
and took the men.

177
00:11:20.569 --> 00:11:22.303
<i>Joffrey killed my father.</i>

178
00:11:22.337 --> 00:11:24.772
your liege lord.

179
00:11:24.806 --> 00:11:27.274
Do you remember
your vows. Ser?

180
00:11:27.308 --> 00:11:29.176
Of course I remember!

181
00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:32.279
We can spare four masons
for a week. My Lord.

182
00:11:32.313 --> 00:11:35.349
Will that be sufficient
to repair your walls?

183
00:11:35.383 --> 00:11:37.685
I-- I believe it will.

184
00:11:43.626 --> 00:11:45.995
We didn't want him here
all day. did we?

185
00:11:47.264 --> 00:11:50.299
I didn't like the way
he was talking about Robb.

186
00:11:50.334 --> 00:11:52.134
Nor did I.

187
00:11:54.404 --> 00:11:57.272
But listening to people
you'd rather not listen to

188
00:11:57.307 --> 00:12:01.377
is one of your responsibilities
as Lord of Winterfell.

189
00:12:04.280 --> 00:12:06.548
<i>Lord Portan.</i>

190
00:12:06.582 --> 00:12:09.617
<i>My Lord. may the Old Gods</i>
<i>watch over your brother</i>

191
00:12:09.651 --> 00:12:11.385
<i>and all our northern sons.</i>

192
00:13:00.337 --> 00:13:04.775
Boil this for an hour
and drink the tea.

193
00:13:04.809 --> 00:13:07.312
Makes all your pain
go away.

194
00:13:07.346 --> 00:13:09.981
Don't have any pain.

195
00:13:10.015 --> 00:13:11.615
Lucky for you.

196
00:13:12.684 --> 00:13:14.518
That way.

197
00:13:17.255 --> 00:13:19.490
You've been having
those dreams again.

198
00:13:19.524 --> 00:13:21.358
<i>I don't dream.</i>

199
00:13:21.392 --> 00:13:22.926
Everyone dreams.

200
00:13:22.960 --> 00:13:25.895
I don't.

201
00:13:25.929 --> 00:13:27.997
Heard some of the men
talking about the comet.

202
00:13:28.031 --> 00:13:30.166
<i>They say it's an omen.</i>

203
00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:33.870
They say it means Robb will win
a great victory in the South.

204
00:13:33.904 --> 00:13:35.505
Did they?

205
00:13:37.274 --> 00:13:40.844
I heard some other fools
say it's Lannister Red.

206
00:13:40.879 --> 00:13:44.248
Means the Lannisters will rule
all Seven Kingdoms before long.

207
00:13:44.282 --> 00:13:47.685
Heard a stableboy say
it's the color of blood

208
00:13:47.719 --> 00:13:50.088
to mark the death
of your father.

209
00:13:53.926 --> 00:13:57.161
The stars
don't fall for men.

210
00:13:57.195 --> 00:13:59.763
The red comet means
one thing. boy--

211
00:14:00.898 --> 00:14:02.499
dragons.

212
00:14:04.335 --> 00:14:07.069
The dragons are all dead.

213
00:14:07.104 --> 00:14:09.572
They've been dead
for centuries.

214
00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:47.878
Mmm.

215
00:14:47.912 --> 00:14:50.847
Mmm. Mmm.

216
00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:55.585
What did your brother say
about them. Khaleesi?

217
00:14:55.619 --> 00:14:57.287
He said they ate meat.

218
00:14:57.322 --> 00:15:01.024
He didn't tell you
what kind of meat?

219
00:15:01.058 --> 00:15:03.960
My brother didn't know
anything about dragons.

220
00:15:03.994 --> 00:15:07.129
He didn't know anything
about anything.

221
00:15:12.069 --> 00:15:14.604
Eh.

222
00:15:40.933 --> 00:15:43.001
She was Drogo's
first gift to me.

223
00:15:43.035 --> 00:15:46.037
I remember.

224
00:15:47.906 --> 00:15:50.542
I promised
to protect them.

225
00:15:50.576 --> 00:15:52.910
Promised them their enemies
would die screaming.

226
00:15:52.945 --> 00:15:55.446
How do I make
starvation scream?

227
00:15:55.481 --> 00:15:58.483
A trick I never learned.
I'm afraid.

228
00:16:00.319 --> 00:16:02.386
Does it ever end?

229
00:16:02.421 --> 00:16:04.388
This is farther east
than I've ever been.

230
00:16:04.422 --> 00:16:05.956
But. yes. Khaleesi.

231
00:16:05.991 --> 00:16:07.458
everything ends.
even the red waste.

232
00:16:07.492 --> 00:16:10.060
And you're sure
there's no other way?

233
00:16:10.095 --> 00:16:12.830
If we go south to the land
of the Lazarheen.

234
00:16:12.864 --> 00:16:15.332
the Lamb Men will kill us
and take your dragons.

235
00:16:15.367 --> 00:16:17.267
If we go west
to the Dothraki Sea.

236
00:16:17.302 --> 00:16:19.336
the first
Khalasar we meet

237
00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:20.904
will kill us
and take your dragons.

238
00:16:20.938 --> 00:16:23.607
No one will take
my dragons.

239
00:16:24.776 --> 00:16:27.478
They are too weak to fight.

240
00:16:27.512 --> 00:16:29.513
as are your people.

241
00:16:29.547 --> 00:16:31.883
You must be
their strength.

242
00:16:32.818 --> 00:16:34.953
As you are mine.

243
00:17:21.933 --> 00:17:24.869
Rakharo...

244
00:17:31.377 --> 00:17:34.146
You never have.

245
00:17:38.984 --> 00:17:42.820
This is bad time to start.

246
00:18:38.912 --> 00:18:40.880
Having a rough time of it?

247
00:18:40.914 --> 00:18:42.481
Nothing's killed me yet.

248
00:18:42.516 --> 00:18:45.084
- Your ass killed the sledge.
- You offered me a ride.

249
00:18:45.119 --> 00:18:48.354
I just wanted you to shut up about
your damn blisters.

250
00:19:02.368 --> 00:19:05.170
I was born in a place
like this.

251
00:19:05.205 --> 00:19:08.340
Later. I fell
on hard times.

252
00:19:09.976 --> 00:19:11.743
<i>Are those girls?</i>

253
00:19:11.777 --> 00:19:13.578
<i>Craster's daughters.</i>

254
00:19:13.613 --> 00:19:17.349
I haven't seen a girl
in six months.

255
00:19:17.383 --> 00:19:19.318
I'd keep on not seeing them
if I were you.

256
00:19:19.352 --> 00:19:22.754
What. he don't like people messing
with his daughters?

257
00:19:22.789 --> 00:19:25.591
He don't like people
messing with his wives.

258
00:19:26.960 --> 00:19:29.194
He marries
his daughters.

259
00:19:29.229 --> 00:19:31.564
<i>and they give him</i>
<i>more daughters.</i>

260
00:19:31.598 --> 00:19:33.799
And on and on it goes.

261
00:19:33.834 --> 00:19:36.268
- That's foul.
- It's beyond foul.

262
00:19:36.302 --> 00:19:40.206
All the other wildlings for a
hundred leagues have disappeared.

263
00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:42.207
Craster's still here.

264
00:19:42.242 --> 00:19:44.877
He must be doing
something right.

265
00:19:46.513 --> 00:19:48.214
What happens
to the boys?

266
00:19:48.248 --> 00:19:51.283
- Hmm?
- <i>He marries his daughters.</i>

267
00:19:51.318 --> 00:19:54.220
What does he do
with his sons?

268
00:19:56.557 --> 00:19:59.258
He said he planned
to stop here

269
00:19:59.293 --> 00:20:00.860
on his way
to the Frostfangs.

270
00:20:00.894 --> 00:20:02.495
People make
all sorts of plans.

271
00:20:02.529 --> 00:20:05.965
I haven't seen Benjen Stark
in three years.

272
00:20:05.999 --> 00:20:07.466
Haven't missed him.

273
00:20:07.501 --> 00:20:10.236
Always treated me
like scum.

274
00:20:11.505 --> 00:20:14.140
Haven't had any good wine
for a long time.

275
00:20:14.174 --> 00:20:17.176
You Southerners make good wine.
I'll give you that.

276
00:20:17.210 --> 00:20:19.245
We're not Southerners.

277
00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:21.014
Who's this little girl?

278
00:20:22.483 --> 00:20:25.285
You're prettier
than half my daughters.

279
00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:28.655
You got a nice wet twat
between your legs?

280
00:20:28.689 --> 00:20:30.423
What's your name?

281
00:20:30.458 --> 00:20:32.458
- Jon Snow.
- Snow. eh?

282
00:20:32.493 --> 00:20:35.327
Listen to me. bastard.

283
00:20:35.362 --> 00:20:39.331
All you lot from south of the Wall.
you're Southerners.

284
00:20:39.365 --> 00:20:43.235
But now you're in the North.
the real North.

285
00:20:43.269 --> 00:20:44.869
The lad meant no harm.

286
00:20:46.372 --> 00:20:49.607
I catch that pretty little bastard
talking to my daughters--

287
00:20:49.642 --> 00:20:53.779
No one will talk to your daughters.
you have my word.

288
00:20:53.813 --> 00:20:57.150
Now. sit down
and shut your mouth.

289
00:20:59.854 --> 00:21:02.156
You bring any of that
good wine with you?

290
00:21:02.190 --> 00:21:04.025
We did.

291
00:21:04.059 --> 00:21:06.561
We passed through
six villages on the way here.

292
00:21:06.595 --> 00:21:08.429
All six were abandoned.

293
00:21:08.464 --> 00:21:11.532
Where have all
the wildlings gone?

294
00:21:11.566 --> 00:21:15.102
I could tell you.
but I'm thirsty.

295
00:21:15.136 --> 00:21:17.238
<i>There's a barrel of</i>
<i>Dornish wine on the sledge.</i>

296
00:21:17.272 --> 00:21:20.007
- <i>Bring it in here.</i>
<i>- Yes. commander.</i>

297
00:21:20.041 --> 00:21:23.210
<i>You want to know</i>
<i>where they've all gone?</i>

298
00:21:23.244 --> 00:21:27.547
<i>North... to join up</i>
<i>with Mance Rayder...</i>

299
00:21:28.716 --> 00:21:30.449
Your old friend.

300
00:21:30.484 --> 00:21:33.119
He's no friend of mine.

301
00:21:33.154 --> 00:21:36.286
He broke his vows.
betrayed his brothers.

302
00:21:36.311 --> 00:21:37.511
Oh. aye.

303
00:21:37.625 --> 00:21:40.695
But once he was
just a poor black crow.

304
00:21:40.729 --> 00:21:43.665
And now he's
King-Beyond-the-Wall.

305
00:21:43.700 --> 00:21:46.168
He's been calling
himself that for years.

306
00:21:46.202 --> 00:21:49.939
What's he king of?
A frozen lake somewhere?

307
00:21:51.308 --> 00:21:53.376
That's a good-looking axe.

308
00:21:53.410 --> 00:21:55.545
<i>Fresh forged?</i>

309
00:21:57.548 --> 00:22:00.083
Give it here.

310
00:22:00.117 --> 00:22:02.285
You'll have another one
made at Castle Black.

311
00:22:02.320 --> 00:22:04.221
Here.

312
00:22:04.255 --> 00:22:08.058
Oh. that's some
lovely steel.

313
00:22:11.762 --> 00:22:14.898
You want to know
what Mance Rayder is doing?

314
00:22:14.932 --> 00:22:16.733
Gathering an army.

315
00:22:16.801 --> 00:22:19.002
<i>What I hear.</i>
<i>he's already got more men</i>

316
00:22:19.036 --> 00:22:21.338
<i>than any of your</i>
<i>southern kings.</i>

317
00:22:21.372 --> 00:22:23.874
And where does he plan
marching this army?

318
00:22:23.908 --> 00:22:25.375
When you're
all the way north.

319
00:22:25.409 --> 00:22:27.144
there's only
one direction to go.

320
00:22:29.347 --> 00:22:33.984
These are bad times to be
living alone in the wild.

321
00:22:34.019 --> 00:22:37.321
The cold winds
are rising.

322
00:22:37.356 --> 00:22:40.858
Let them come.
My roots are sunk deep.

323
00:22:42.361 --> 00:22:44.361
Wife...

324
00:22:44.396 --> 00:22:48.432
tell the Lord Crow
how content we are.

325
00:22:48.466 --> 00:22:50.834
This is our place.

326
00:22:50.868 --> 00:22:52.769
Our husband keeps us safe.

327
00:22:52.804 --> 00:22:55.973
Better to live free
than die a slave.

328
00:22:57.742 --> 00:23:01.245
<i>Don't it make you</i>
<i>jealous. old man.</i>

329
00:23:01.279 --> 00:23:03.347
to see me with
all these young wives

330
00:23:03.381 --> 00:23:06.650
and you with no one
to warm your bed?

331
00:23:06.684 --> 00:23:08.619
We chose different paths.

332
00:23:08.653 --> 00:23:13.090
Oh. aye. and you chose the path
with no one but boys on it.

333
00:23:14.959 --> 00:23:18.094
You'll be wanting to sleep
beneath my roof. I suppose.

334
00:23:18.129 --> 00:23:20.196
and eat me out of pigs.

335
00:23:20.231 --> 00:23:22.132
A roof would be welcome.

336
00:23:22.166 --> 00:23:23.700
It's been hard riding.

337
00:23:23.734 --> 00:23:26.936
We've brought our own food
and good steel for you.

338
00:23:29.540 --> 00:23:32.275
Any man lays a hand
on one of my wives.

339
00:23:32.309 --> 00:23:35.278
he loses the hand.

340
00:23:37.114 --> 00:23:40.916
And I see this one
staring too long.

341
00:23:40.951 --> 00:23:44.186
I might just gouge
his eyes out.

342
00:23:44.220 --> 00:23:47.490
Your roof. your rules.

343
00:24:00.472 --> 00:24:02.773
Who am I?!

344
00:24:02.808 --> 00:24:06.244
- Who am I?!
- Lord commander.

345
00:24:06.278 --> 00:24:09.447
- And who are you?
- Jon Snow.

346
00:24:09.481 --> 00:24:12.083
Who <i>are</i> you?

347
00:24:12.117 --> 00:24:14.385
Your steward.

348
00:24:14.419 --> 00:24:16.520
You want to lead
one day?

349
00:24:19.290 --> 00:24:22.025
Then learn
how to follow.

350
00:24:39.544 --> 00:24:44.281
<i>Lord of Light. come to us</i>
<i>in our darkness.</i>

351
00:24:44.315 --> 00:24:48.019
We offer you
these false Gods.

352
00:24:48.053 --> 00:24:50.988
Take them and cast
your light upon us...

353
00:24:52.691 --> 00:24:56.727
For the night is dark
and full of terrors.

354
00:24:56.761 --> 00:25:00.263
For the night is dark
and full of terrors.

355
00:25:02.232 --> 00:25:04.166
<i>After the long summer.</i>

356
00:25:04.200 --> 00:25:07.236
<i>darkness will fall heavy</i>
<i>on the world.</i>

357
00:25:07.270 --> 00:25:09.972
The stars will bleed.

358
00:25:10.006 --> 00:25:12.375
We need to stop her.

359
00:25:12.409 --> 00:25:16.212
<i>The cold breath of winter</i>
<i>will freeze the seas...</i>

360
00:25:16.246 --> 00:25:17.644
Not now.

361
00:25:17.669 --> 00:25:18.869
<i>...And the dead shall rise</i>
<i>in the North.</i>

362
00:25:22.419 --> 00:25:25.989
All you men were named
in the Light of the Seven!

363
00:25:26.024 --> 00:25:29.159
<i>Is this how you treat</i>
<i>the Gods of your fathers?</i>

364
00:25:29.194 --> 00:25:33.897
Are you so eager to spit
on your ancestors?

365
00:25:42.472 --> 00:25:44.906
You smell of fear--

366
00:25:44.974 --> 00:25:49.210
fear and piss
and old bones.

367
00:25:50.445 --> 00:25:52.146
Do you want to stop me?

368
00:25:56.585 --> 00:25:58.452
Stop me.

369
00:26:11.267 --> 00:26:13.001
In the ancient books.
it's written

370
00:26:13.036 --> 00:26:17.072
that a warrior will draw
a burning sword from the fire.

371
00:26:18.208 --> 00:26:21.276
And that sword shall be
Lightbringer.

372
00:26:26.083 --> 00:26:29.585
Stannis Baratheon.

373
00:26:29.619 --> 00:26:32.187
warrior of light.

374
00:26:32.222 --> 00:26:34.123
your sword awaits you.

375
00:27:04.389 --> 00:27:07.858
Lord. cast your
light upon us!

376
00:27:09.393 --> 00:27:12.729
<i>For the night is dark</i>
<i>and full of terrors.</i>

377
00:27:15.566 --> 00:27:19.035
For the night is dark
and full of terror.

378
00:27:46.097 --> 00:27:49.732
This woman will lead him
into a war he cannot win.

379
00:27:49.767 --> 00:27:51.400
Stannis is our king.

380
00:27:51.435 --> 00:27:52.768
We follow
where he leads.

381
00:27:52.803 --> 00:27:55.504
- even if we don't like the path.
- King.

382
00:27:55.538 --> 00:27:57.639
Since that boar
killed his brother.

383
00:27:57.674 --> 00:27:59.708
every lord wants
a coronation.

384
00:27:59.742 --> 00:28:01.843
I don't serve the others.
I serve Stannis.

385
00:28:01.878 --> 00:28:05.580
As do I.
but loyal service

386
00:28:05.614 --> 00:28:08.550
means telling
hard truths.

387
00:28:08.584 --> 00:28:12.653
He's surrounded
by fools and fanatics.

388
00:28:12.688 --> 00:28:15.456
but he trusts you. Davos.

389
00:28:15.491 --> 00:28:18.593
If you tell him
the truth...

390
00:28:19.996 --> 00:28:21.931
What's the truth?

391
00:28:34.578 --> 00:28:36.379
<i>"And I declare upon</i>
<i>the honor of my house</i>

392
00:28:36.413 --> 00:28:37.847
<i>that my beloved</i>
<i>brother Robert--"</i>

393
00:28:37.881 --> 00:28:40.483
he wasn't
my beloved brother.

394
00:28:40.517 --> 00:28:42.718
I didn't love him.
He didn't love me.

395
00:28:42.753 --> 00:28:44.587
A harmless courtesy.
Your Grace.

396
00:28:44.621 --> 00:28:45.988
A lie.
Take it out.

397
00:28:48.925 --> 00:28:50.826
"...that my brother Robert
left no trueborn heirs.

398
00:28:50.860 --> 00:28:53.262
the boy Joffrey.
the boy Tommen.

399
00:28:53.296 --> 00:28:55.464
and the girl Myrcella
being born of incest

400
00:28:55.499 --> 00:28:58.502
<i>between Cersei Lannister and</i>
<i>her brother Jaime Lannister.</i>

401
00:28:58.536 --> 00:29:01.438
- <i>By right of birth--"</i>
- Jaime Lannister. the Kingslayer.

402
00:29:01.472 --> 00:29:04.274
Call him what he is.

403
00:29:04.309 --> 00:29:05.809
<i>"...And her brother</i>
<i>Jaime Lannister.</i>

404
00:29:05.844 --> 00:29:07.211
<i>the Kingslayer.</i>

405
00:29:07.246 --> 00:29:10.482
<i>By right of birth and blood.</i>
<i>i do this day lay claim--"</i>

406
00:29:10.516 --> 00:29:13.651
<i>Make it</i> Ser <i>Jaime Lannister.</i>
<i>the Kingslayer.</i>

407
00:29:13.686 --> 00:29:15.887
Whatever else he is.
the man's still a knight.

408
00:29:15.922 --> 00:29:17.956
"Ser Jaime Lannister.
the Kingslayer.

409
00:29:17.990 --> 00:29:20.325
By right of birth
and blood.

410
00:29:20.359 --> 00:29:23.796
<i>I do this day lay claim</i>
<i>to the Iron Throne of Westeros.</i>

411
00:29:23.830 --> 00:29:26.331
Let all true men
declare their loyalty."

412
00:29:26.366 --> 00:29:28.700
When Eddard Stark learned
the truth. he told only me.

413
00:29:28.735 --> 00:29:31.136
I'll not make
the same mistake.

414
00:29:31.170 --> 00:29:33.205
Send copies of that letter
to every corner of the Realm.

415
00:29:33.239 --> 00:29:35.106
from the Arbor
to the Wall.

416
00:29:35.141 --> 00:29:38.043
The time has come
to choose.

417
00:29:38.077 --> 00:29:40.545
Let no man claim ignorance
as an excuse.

418
00:29:40.580 --> 00:29:43.181
Your Grace.the Lannisters
are the true enemy.

419
00:29:43.216 --> 00:29:45.250
If. for the time being. you could
make peace with your brother--

420
00:29:45.284 --> 00:29:47.552
I'll not make peace with Renly
while he calls himself King.

421
00:29:47.587 --> 00:29:49.421
Well. many have already
declared for him--

422
00:29:49.455 --> 00:29:51.590
Mace Tyrell.
Randyll Tarly.

423
00:29:51.625 --> 00:29:54.860
Stannis does not need to beg
this lord or that lord for support.

424
00:29:54.894 --> 00:29:56.462
<i>The Lord of Light</i>
<i>stands behind him.</i>

425
00:29:56.496 --> 00:29:59.965
And how many ships has
the Lord of Light got in his fleet?

426
00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:02.568
- He has no need for ships.
- I'm sure he doesn't.

427
00:30:02.602 --> 00:30:04.003
but we do if we're
going to war.

428
00:30:04.037 --> 00:30:07.106
If not Renly. Your Grace.
join forces with Robb Stark.

429
00:30:07.140 --> 00:30:09.442
Who would steal
the northern half of my kingdom.

430
00:30:09.476 --> 00:30:10.777
I've always served thieves
according to their desserts.

431
00:30:10.811 --> 00:30:12.946
<i>as you well know.</i>
<i>Ser Davos.</i>

432
00:30:12.980 --> 00:30:15.981
Joffrey. Renly. Robb Stark.
they're all thieves.

433
00:30:16.016 --> 00:30:18.484
They'll bend the knee
or I'll destroy them.

434
00:30:18.518 --> 00:30:23.088
I owe you
an apology. my King.

435
00:30:23.123 --> 00:30:25.191
My duty is to serve.

436
00:30:25.225 --> 00:30:29.294
<i>You have chosen the new God</i>
<i>over the Old Gods.</i>

437
00:30:29.329 --> 00:30:32.831
<i>May the Lord of Light</i>
<i>watch over us all.</i>

438
00:30:32.866 --> 00:30:35.233
Shall we drink together?

439
00:30:35.268 --> 00:30:37.269
Don't.

440
00:30:37.303 --> 00:30:42.108
A cup of wine to honor
the one true God.

441
00:31:28.225 --> 00:31:31.427
The night is dark and full
of terrors. old man.

442
00:31:31.462 --> 00:31:34.697
but the fire
burns them all away.

443
00:31:56.253 --> 00:31:58.254
Your Grace.

444
00:32:09.634 --> 00:32:12.303
King in the North.

445
00:32:14.239 --> 00:32:16.040
I keep expecting you
to leave me

446
00:32:16.075 --> 00:32:18.109
in one castle or another
for safekeeping.

447
00:32:18.144 --> 00:32:22.180
but you drag me along
from camp to camp.

448
00:32:22.214 --> 00:32:24.849
Have you grown
fond of me. Stark?

449
00:32:24.884 --> 00:32:26.684
Is that it?

450
00:32:26.719 --> 00:32:28.720
I've never seen you
with a girl.

451
00:32:29.822 --> 00:32:32.257
If I left you with
one of my bannermen.

452
00:32:32.291 --> 00:32:35.327
your father would know
within a fortnight

453
00:32:35.361 --> 00:32:38.831
and my bannerman would receive
a raven with a message:

454
00:32:38.865 --> 00:32:42.434
"Release my son and you'll be rich
beyond your dreams.

455
00:32:42.469 --> 00:32:46.005
Refuse and your house
will be destroyed. root and stem."

456
00:32:46.039 --> 00:32:48.340
You don't trust
the loyalty

457
00:32:48.375 --> 00:32:50.676
of the men following
you into battle?

458
00:32:50.711 --> 00:32:54.214
Oh. I trust them
with my life.

459
00:32:54.248 --> 00:32:56.249
just not with yours.

460
00:32:56.283 --> 00:32:58.117
Smart boy.

461
00:32:58.152 --> 00:32:59.786
What's wrong?

462
00:32:59.820 --> 00:33:01.787
<i>Don't like</i>
<i>being called "boy"?</i>

463
00:33:02.722 --> 00:33:04.757
Insulted?

464
00:33:11.731 --> 00:33:14.599
<i>You insult yourself.</i>
<i>Kingslayer.</i>

465
00:33:16.268 --> 00:33:19.670
<i>You've been defeated by a boy.</i>

466
00:33:19.705 --> 00:33:22.172
<i>You're held captive</i>
<i>by a boy.</i>

467
00:33:24.275 --> 00:33:26.877
<i>Perhaps you'll be</i>
<i>killed by a boy.</i>

468
00:33:33.618 --> 00:33:35.386
Stannis Baratheon
sent ravens

469
00:33:35.421 --> 00:33:38.790
to all the high lords
of Westeros.

470
00:33:38.825 --> 00:33:42.495
King Joffrey Baratheon
is neither a true king

471
00:33:42.529 --> 00:33:45.164
<i>nor a true Baratheon.</i>

472
00:33:45.199 --> 00:33:47.333
He's your bastard son.

473
00:33:47.368 --> 00:33:49.937
<i>If that's true.</i>
<i>Stannis is the rightful king.</i>

474
00:33:49.971 --> 00:33:52.005
How convenient for him.

475
00:33:52.039 --> 00:33:56.309
My father learned
the truth.

476
00:33:56.344 --> 00:33:58.011
That's why
you had him executed.

477
00:33:58.046 --> 00:34:00.414
I was your prisoner
when Ned Stark lost his head.

478
00:34:00.448 --> 00:34:02.550
Your son killed him

479
00:34:02.584 --> 00:34:04.018
so the world wouldn't
learn who fathered him.

480
00:34:04.052 --> 00:34:08.089
And you-- you pushed
my brother from a window

481
00:34:08.123 --> 00:34:10.091
because he saw you
with the queen.

482
00:34:15.264 --> 00:34:18.300
You have proof?

483
00:34:18.334 --> 00:34:20.836
Or do you want to trade gossip
like a couple of fishwives?

484
00:34:20.871 --> 00:34:23.039
I'm sending one of your cousins
down to King's Landing

485
00:34:23.074 --> 00:34:24.708
with my peace terms.

486
00:34:24.742 --> 00:34:27.778
You think my father's going
to negotiate with you?

487
00:34:27.812 --> 00:34:30.214
You don't know him
very well.

488
00:34:30.248 --> 00:34:34.618
No. but he's starting
to know me.

489
00:34:34.652 --> 00:34:38.287
<i>Three victories</i>
<i>don't make you a conqueror.</i>

490
00:34:39.756 --> 00:34:42.391
It's better than
three defeats.

491
00:35:10.823 --> 00:35:13.424
<i>This city stinks...</i>

492
00:35:15.828 --> 00:35:17.395
Like dead bodies.

493
00:35:17.429 --> 00:35:19.563
<i>A bit corpsey. yes.</i>

494
00:35:19.597 --> 00:35:22.065
And shit.

495
00:35:22.100 --> 00:35:24.000
I thought you wanted
to come here.

496
00:35:27.337 --> 00:35:29.705
I love it.

497
00:35:29.739 --> 00:35:33.409
You love the smell
of dead bodies and shit?

498
00:35:33.443 --> 00:35:36.479
And cum and garlic
and rum.

499
00:35:36.513 --> 00:35:39.649
You can smell cum
from the balcony?

500
00:35:39.683 --> 00:35:43.020
I love the stink.
I love the noise.

501
00:35:43.054 --> 00:35:45.156
Cities make me
want to fuck.

502
00:35:45.190 --> 00:35:48.493
And so did the country.

503
00:35:51.597 --> 00:35:53.097
This is where I belong.

504
00:35:53.132 --> 00:35:56.000
Yes. well. you need
to be careful.

505
00:35:56.034 --> 00:35:57.601
No one can know
you're here.

506
00:35:57.636 --> 00:35:59.303
No one will know.

507
00:35:59.337 --> 00:36:00.904
You can't trust anyone
in King's Landing.

508
00:36:00.939 --> 00:36:04.107
<i>They're all liars--</i>
<i>good liars. bad liars.</i>

509
00:36:04.142 --> 00:36:06.576
one or two great liars.

510
00:36:06.610 --> 00:36:08.611
What about you?

511
00:36:08.645 --> 00:36:11.280
Me? I'm not from here.
I'm a slave to the truth.

512
00:36:11.314 --> 00:36:14.116
Truth?

513
00:36:15.919 --> 00:36:19.088
You are the biggest
little liar I have ever met.

514
00:36:19.122 --> 00:36:21.123
Why do you think
I am so little?

515
00:36:21.157 --> 00:36:25.693
I'm being crushed beneath the
weight of all that truth.

516
00:36:27.863 --> 00:36:29.830
Oh!

517
00:36:29.865 --> 00:36:32.667
Ned Stark actually
slept on this.

518
00:36:32.701 --> 00:36:36.538
As if the poor man
didn't suffer enough.

519
00:36:38.341 --> 00:36:41.811
One of the many changes
we'll have to make around here.

520
00:36:52.989 --> 00:36:56.291
- Lord Baelish.
- Your Grace.

521
00:36:56.326 --> 00:36:58.894
I wonder if I might
ask you for a favor.

522
00:36:58.928 --> 00:37:00.429
Of course.
Your Grace.

523
00:37:00.463 --> 00:37:02.397
Ned Stark's youngest
daughter Arya--

524
00:37:02.432 --> 00:37:04.633
we can't seem
to locate her.

525
00:37:04.667 --> 00:37:07.168
If she's escaped
the capital.

526
00:37:07.203 --> 00:37:09.270
Winterfell seems
the logical destination.

527
00:37:09.304 --> 00:37:11.840
And yet my friends in the North
report no sign of her.

528
00:37:11.874 --> 00:37:13.808
Curious.

529
00:37:13.843 --> 00:37:15.977
If we choose to negotiate
with the Starks.

530
00:37:16.012 --> 00:37:18.280
the girl has some value.
Whoever finds her--

531
00:37:18.314 --> 00:37:20.849
well. you know what they say about
Lannisters and debts.

532
00:37:20.884 --> 00:37:22.885
Well. you could ask
Varys where she is.

533
00:37:22.920 --> 00:37:25.221
He'll have
an answer for you.

534
00:37:25.256 --> 00:37:26.823
Whether you believe it...

535
00:37:26.857 --> 00:37:30.728
Myself. I have always had
a hard time trusting eunuchs.

536
00:37:30.762 --> 00:37:33.397
Who knows what they want?

537
00:37:33.431 --> 00:37:36.533
A mockingbird.

538
00:37:36.568 --> 00:37:38.327
You created your
own Sigil. didn't you?

539
00:37:38.352 --> 00:37:39.552
Yes.

540
00:37:40.104 --> 00:37:42.406
Appropriate...
for a self-made man

541
00:37:42.440 --> 00:37:44.174
with so many
songs to sing.

542
00:37:44.208 --> 00:37:45.842
I'm glad you like it.

543
00:37:45.877 --> 00:37:47.745
Some people are
fortunate enough

544
00:37:47.779 --> 00:37:49.412
to be born into
the right family.

545
00:37:49.447 --> 00:37:52.115
Others have to find
their own way.

546
00:37:53.484 --> 00:37:55.518
I heard a song once

547
00:37:55.552 --> 00:37:58.187
about a boy
of modest means

548
00:37:58.221 --> 00:38:01.957
who found his way into the
home of a very prominent family.

549
00:38:01.991 --> 00:38:03.759
He loved
the eldest daughter.

550
00:38:03.793 --> 00:38:07.196
Sadly. she had eyes
for another.

551
00:38:07.230 --> 00:38:09.598
When boys and girls
live in the same home.

552
00:38:09.632 --> 00:38:12.267
awkward situations
can arise.

553
00:38:12.301 --> 00:38:14.936
Sometimes. I've heard.
even brothers and sisters

554
00:38:14.970 --> 00:38:17.471
develop
certain affections.

555
00:38:17.506 --> 00:38:19.940
And when these affections
become common knowledge.

556
00:38:19.974 --> 00:38:23.843
well. that is an awkward
situation indeed.

557
00:38:23.878 --> 00:38:26.179
especially
in a prominent family.

558
00:38:26.213 --> 00:38:29.649
But prominent families
often forget a simple truth.

559
00:38:29.683 --> 00:38:31.918
I've found.

560
00:38:31.952 --> 00:38:34.087
And which truth is that?

561
00:38:34.121 --> 00:38:37.758
Knowledge is power.

562
00:38:39.928 --> 00:38:42.330
Seize him.

563
00:38:44.166 --> 00:38:46.168
Cut his throat.

564
00:38:47.303 --> 00:38:49.772
Stop. Wait.

565
00:38:49.806 --> 00:38:52.175
I've changed my mind.
Let him go.

566
00:38:55.112 --> 00:38:56.812
Step back three paces.

567
00:38:58.215 --> 00:39:00.616
Turn around.

568
00:39:00.650 --> 00:39:02.317
Close your eyes.

569
00:39:06.523 --> 00:39:08.958
Power is power.

570
00:39:10.693 --> 00:39:12.180
Do see if you can
take some time away from

571
00:39:12.205 --> 00:39:14.119
your coins and your whores

572
00:39:14.464 --> 00:39:16.265
to locate
the Stark girl for me.

573
00:39:16.299 --> 00:39:19.835
I would very much
appreciate it.

574
00:39:29.646 --> 00:39:31.847
<i>You're Ser Alton Lannister?</i>

575
00:39:31.881 --> 00:39:34.450
I am. Your Grace.

576
00:39:34.484 --> 00:39:38.021
<i>I offer your cousins peace</i>
<i>if they meet my terms.</i>

577
00:39:38.055 --> 00:39:42.358
First. your family
must release my sisters.

578
00:39:42.393 --> 00:39:46.061
Second. my father's bones
must be returned to us

579
00:39:46.095 --> 00:39:48.029
so he may rest beside
his brother and sister

580
00:39:48.064 --> 00:39:50.799
in the crypts
beneath Winterfell.

581
00:39:50.833 --> 00:39:53.002
And the remains of all those
who died in his service

582
00:39:53.036 --> 00:39:55.237
must also be returned.

583
00:39:55.272 --> 00:39:57.774
Their families can honor
them with proper funerals.

584
00:39:57.809 --> 00:40:00.877
- An honorable request. Your Grace.
- <i>Third...</i>

585
00:40:02.547 --> 00:40:05.016
Joffrey and the Queen Regent
must renounce all claim

586
00:40:05.050 --> 00:40:07.652
to dominion of the North.

587
00:40:07.687 --> 00:40:09.888
From this time
till the end of time.

588
00:40:09.923 --> 00:40:12.457
we are a free
and independent kingdom.

589
00:40:12.492 --> 00:40:14.459
The King in the North.

590
00:40:14.494 --> 00:40:16.961
King in the North.

591
00:40:16.996 --> 00:40:18.563
Neither Joffrey
nor any of his men

592
00:40:18.598 --> 00:40:20.832
shall set foot
in our lands again.

593
00:40:20.900 --> 00:40:22.767
If he disregards
this command.

594
00:40:22.802 --> 00:40:26.338
he shall suffer
the same fate as my father.

595
00:40:26.372 --> 00:40:30.675
only I don't need a servant
to do my beheading for me.

596
00:40:30.709 --> 00:40:34.212
These are-- Your Grace.
these are--

597
00:40:34.246 --> 00:40:36.781
these are my terms.

598
00:40:36.815 --> 00:40:39.951
If the Queen Regent and her son
meet them. I'll give them peace.

599
00:40:39.985 --> 00:40:42.954
If not...

600
00:40:42.988 --> 00:40:45.423
I will litter the south
with Lannister dead.

601
00:40:45.458 --> 00:40:48.360
King Joffrey is a Baratheon.
Your Grace.

602
00:40:48.394 --> 00:40:50.195
Oh. is he?

603
00:40:51.398 --> 00:40:54.733
You'll ride at daybreak.
Ser Alton.

604
00:40:54.768 --> 00:40:57.402
That will be all
for tonight.

605
00:41:12.151 --> 00:41:14.286
A word. Your Grace?

606
00:41:16.055 --> 00:41:18.790
You don't have to call me
"Your Grace" when no one's around.

607
00:41:18.824 --> 00:41:21.527
It's not so bad
once you get used to it.

608
00:41:21.561 --> 00:41:23.395
I'm glad someone's
gotten used to it.

609
00:41:23.429 --> 00:41:26.765
The Lannisters are going to reject
your terms. you know?

610
00:41:26.799 --> 00:41:28.500
Of course they are.

611
00:41:28.534 --> 00:41:30.869
We can fight them
in the fields as long as you like.

612
00:41:30.903 --> 00:41:34.606
but we won't beat them until you
take King's Landing.

613
00:41:36.142 --> 00:41:39.278
And we can't take
King's Landing without ships.

614
00:41:39.312 --> 00:41:41.947
My father has ships and men
who know how to sail them.

615
00:41:41.982 --> 00:41:43.749
Men who fought
my father.

616
00:41:43.784 --> 00:41:46.218
Men who fought King Robert
to free themselves

617
00:41:46.252 --> 00:41:50.056
from the yoke of the South.
just like you're doing now.

618
00:41:51.224 --> 00:41:54.294
I'm his only living son.

619
00:41:54.328 --> 00:41:57.464
He'll listen to me.
I know he will.

620
00:41:59.900 --> 00:42:03.169
I'm not a Stark.
I know that.

621
00:42:03.204 --> 00:42:06.173
But your father raised me
to be an honorable man.

622
00:42:07.942 --> 00:42:10.444
We can avenge him
together.

623
00:42:11.746 --> 00:42:14.715
You don't want
Balon Greyjoy for an ally.

624
00:42:14.749 --> 00:42:17.017
I need his ships.
They say he has 200.

625
00:42:17.052 --> 00:42:20.621
They say a million rats
live in the sewers of King's Landing.

626
00:42:20.655 --> 00:42:22.590
Shall we rally them
to fight for us?

627
00:42:22.624 --> 00:42:24.458
I understand you don't
trust Lord Greyjoy.

628
00:42:24.493 --> 00:42:29.163
I don't trust Lord Greyjoy because
he is not trustworthy.

629
00:42:29.197 --> 00:42:31.832
Your father had to go to war
to end his rebellion.

630
00:42:31.867 --> 00:42:35.737
Yes. And now I'm the one
rebelling against the throne.

631
00:42:35.771 --> 00:42:38.039
Before me. it was father.

632
00:42:38.073 --> 00:42:39.740
You married one rebel
and mothered another.

633
00:42:39.774 --> 00:42:42.777
I mothered more than
just rebels.

634
00:42:42.811 --> 00:42:45.145
a fact you seem
to have forgotten.

635
00:42:45.180 --> 00:42:47.181
If I trade the Kingslayer
for two girls.

636
00:42:47.215 --> 00:42:49.482
my bannermen will string me up
by my feet.

637
00:42:49.517 --> 00:42:52.686
You want to leave Sansa
in the Queen's hands?

638
00:42:52.720 --> 00:42:54.788
<i>And Arya--</i>

639
00:42:54.822 --> 00:42:57.824
I haven't heard
a word about Arya.

640
00:42:57.859 --> 00:42:59.593
What are we fighting for
if not for them?

641
00:42:59.627 --> 00:43:01.228
It's more complicated
than that!

642
00:43:01.262 --> 00:43:03.397
You know it is.

643
00:43:17.847 --> 00:43:21.450
It's time for me
to go home.

644
00:43:21.484 --> 00:43:24.386
I haven't seen Bran
or Rickon in months.

645
00:43:25.355 --> 00:43:28.057
You can't go
to Winterfell.

646
00:43:28.091 --> 00:43:30.059
I beg your pardon?

647
00:43:30.093 --> 00:43:33.228
I'll send Rodrik
to watch over the boys

648
00:43:33.263 --> 00:43:37.799
because tomorrow
you'll ride south to the Stormlands.

649
00:43:37.833 --> 00:43:39.834
Why in the name
of all the Gods--

650
00:43:39.868 --> 00:43:43.771
because I need you to negotiate
with Renly Baratheon.

651
00:43:43.806 --> 00:43:45.940
He's rallied
an army of 100.000.

652
00:43:45.975 --> 00:43:47.709
You know him.
You know his family.

653
00:43:47.743 --> 00:43:50.177
I haven't seen Renly Baratheon
since he was a boy.

654
00:43:50.212 --> 00:43:51.746
<i>You have a hundred</i>
<i>other lords--</i>

655
00:43:51.780 --> 00:43:55.650
Which of these lords
do I trust more than you?

656
00:43:55.684 --> 00:43:58.486
If Renly sides with us.

657
00:43:58.521 --> 00:44:00.955
we'll outnumber them
two to one.

658
00:44:00.989 --> 00:44:03.925
When they feel the jaws beginning
to shut. they'll sue for peace.

659
00:44:03.959 --> 00:44:06.694
We'll get the girls back.

660
00:44:06.728 --> 00:44:10.231
Then we'll all
go home... for good.

661
00:44:17.339 --> 00:44:20.308
I will ride at first light.

662
00:44:28.951 --> 00:44:32.553
We will all be together
again soon. I promise.

663
00:44:37.559 --> 00:44:40.160
You've done so well.

664
00:44:41.463 --> 00:44:45.332
Your father
would be... proud.

665
00:44:53.075 --> 00:44:56.077
- Give Lord Renly my regards.
- <i>King</i> Renly.

666
00:44:57.413 --> 00:45:00.182
There's a king
in every corner now.

667
00:45:13.129 --> 00:45:15.663
What is all this?

668
00:45:15.698 --> 00:45:17.966
Returning this room
to its proper appearance.

669
00:45:18.000 --> 00:45:20.868
Say what you will about the Targaryens--
they were conquerors.

670
00:45:20.903 --> 00:45:23.738
That is a seat
for a conqueror.

671
00:45:23.772 --> 00:45:27.441
It needs a room to match it.
not vines and flowers.

672
00:45:27.475 --> 00:45:29.843
We can't find Arya Stark.

673
00:45:29.878 --> 00:45:32.012
With luck. she's dead
in a ditch somewhere.

674
00:45:32.046 --> 00:45:34.014
Perhaps. But if not.
we need her.

675
00:45:34.048 --> 00:45:36.383
They'll never give Jaime back
to us for Sansa alone.

676
00:45:36.418 --> 00:45:39.019
I think they might.
They're weak.

677
00:45:39.054 --> 00:45:40.888
They put too much value
on their women.

678
00:45:40.922 --> 00:45:44.758
We need to set our armies
to the task of finding her.

679
00:45:44.793 --> 00:45:46.660
Send out as many men
as we can.

680
00:45:46.695 --> 00:45:48.496
I'm sure if you asked
grandfather--

681
00:45:48.530 --> 00:45:52.533
The King does not ask;
He commands.

682
00:45:52.567 --> 00:45:55.436
And my grandfather's
stupidity in the field of battle

683
00:45:55.470 --> 00:45:58.372
is the reason Robb Stark has
Uncle Jaime in the first place.

684
00:45:58.406 --> 00:46:01.107
His life is in danger.

685
00:46:01.142 --> 00:46:02.776
We're at war.

686
00:46:02.810 --> 00:46:05.911
All our lives
are in danger.

687
00:46:08.915 --> 00:46:12.418
I heard a disgusting lie
about Uncle Jaime.

688
00:46:12.452 --> 00:46:14.086
And you.

689
00:46:15.255 --> 00:46:16.756
Our enemies
will say anything

690
00:46:16.790 --> 00:46:18.791
to weaken your claim
to the throne.

691
00:46:18.826 --> 00:46:20.961
It's not a claim.
The throne is mine.

692
00:46:22.263 --> 00:46:24.365
Of course it is.

693
00:46:26.335 --> 00:46:28.236
No one believes
this foul gossip.

694
00:46:28.270 --> 00:46:30.405
Someone believes it.

695
00:46:31.741 --> 00:46:34.375
Father had
other children?

696
00:46:34.410 --> 00:46:36.945
Besides me and Tommen
and Myrcella?

697
00:46:38.748 --> 00:46:40.715
What are you asking?

698
00:46:40.749 --> 00:46:43.151
I'm asking if he fucked
other women

699
00:46:43.186 --> 00:46:44.720
when he grew tired
of you.

700
00:46:44.754 --> 00:46:46.555
How many bastards
does he have running--

701
00:47:02.304 --> 00:47:06.540
What you just did
is punishable by death.

702
00:47:09.977 --> 00:47:12.679
You will never
do it again.

703
00:47:12.747 --> 00:47:14.648
Never.

704
00:47:20.688 --> 00:47:22.789
That will be all.
Mother.

705
00:47:29.397 --> 00:47:31.498
No. no. no. no.

706
00:47:31.533 --> 00:47:34.335
Do you have any idea
how ridiculous you sound?

707
00:47:34.369 --> 00:47:35.837
Ease into it.

708
00:47:35.871 --> 00:47:38.873
Slowly. with passion.

709
00:47:38.907 --> 00:47:42.644
Oh. yeah.

710
00:47:42.679 --> 00:47:46.548
Go wash yourselves.
Put some clothes on.

711
00:47:46.583 --> 00:47:49.185
Both of you
are working tonight.

712
00:47:52.955 --> 00:47:54.923
We do things
differently here. Daisy.

713
00:47:54.957 --> 00:47:58.926
This isn't some five-copper
bawdy house in Hayseed Hall.

714
00:47:58.960 --> 00:48:01.461
- Haystack Hall.
- Wherever you're from.

715
00:48:01.496 --> 00:48:03.330
Our establishment
doesn't cater

716
00:48:03.364 --> 00:48:06.132
to ploughmen
and goat herders.

717
00:48:06.166 --> 00:48:08.267
Lord Olsen.

718
00:48:08.301 --> 00:48:10.002
Taste is
everything here.

719
00:48:10.036 --> 00:48:11.904
Littlefinger's
a fancy man.

720
00:48:11.938 --> 00:48:13.706
Don't call him
Littlefinger.

721
00:48:13.741 --> 00:48:15.174
He doesn't like it.

722
00:48:15.209 --> 00:48:17.677
<i>Lord Baelish.</i>

723
00:48:22.884 --> 00:48:25.452
She pretends she doesn't
speak the common tongue

724
00:48:25.487 --> 00:48:28.055
so that people
will think she's exotic.

725
00:48:28.090 --> 00:48:30.992
She grew up just down the road
in flea bottom.

726
00:48:31.027 --> 00:48:33.595
She's beautiful.

727
00:48:33.629 --> 00:48:36.865
She's a dumb slut. really.
but a lid for every pot.

728
00:48:42.037 --> 00:48:44.239
Lord Commander.

729
00:48:44.273 --> 00:48:47.408
Good to see you...
Again.

730
00:49:02.125 --> 00:49:03.859
You do realize
this establishment

731
00:49:03.894 --> 00:49:06.229
is owned by
Lord Petyr Baelish.

732
00:49:06.264 --> 00:49:08.431
the King's
Master of Coin...

733
00:49:08.466 --> 00:49:10.400
Coin which goes
in many pockets.

734
00:49:10.435 --> 00:49:13.137
- Orders.
- Whose orders?

735
00:49:13.171 --> 00:49:16.172
Someone who doesn't care
what Littlefinger thinks.

736
00:49:33.790 --> 00:49:37.326
No. you can't.
No! Please!

737
00:49:37.361 --> 00:49:40.029
No! Not my Barra!

738
00:49:40.063 --> 00:49:43.466
- Please. Please.
- Enough. Get it done.

739
00:49:43.500 --> 00:49:45.534
- <i>Kill the bastard.</i>
<i>- No. no!</i>

740
00:49:45.569 --> 00:49:48.070
- <i>Please.</i>
- Give it here.

741
00:49:48.105 --> 00:49:50.640
No. please.

742
00:50:00.550 --> 00:50:02.885
<i>Spread out.</i>
<i>Search every house.</i>

743
00:50:02.919 --> 00:50:05.487
<i>Every room.</i>
<i>Look in every room.</i>

744
00:50:18.868 --> 00:50:22.003
People shouting )

745
00:50:29.945 --> 00:50:32.446
Gendry!
His name is Gendry.

746
00:50:32.481 --> 00:50:34.348
Where is
the bastard?

747
00:50:34.382 --> 00:50:36.984
The Night's Watch!
Please. stop!

748
00:50:37.018 --> 00:50:38.385
Where?

749
00:50:38.419 --> 00:50:41.388
They took him up the Kingsroad.
heading north.

750
00:50:41.422 --> 00:50:45.024
- How will we know him?
- <i>He's got a bull's head helmet.</i>

751
00:50:45.058 --> 00:50:48.293
- <i>He made it himself.</i>
- Find him.

752
